	"simurail.ponder.physics_bogey.intro.header": "Placing Structures on Train Tracks using Physics Bogies",
	"simurail.ponder.physics_bogey.intro.text_1": "The Physics Bogie attaches Simulated Contraptions to Train Tracks",
	"simurail.ponder.physics_bogey.intro.text_2": "Placing a Physics Bogie on a Train Track while sneaking directly creates a Simulated Contraption...",
	"simurail.ponder.physics_bogey.intro.text_3": "...or you can assemble one with multiple Physics Bogies",
	"simurail.ponder.physics_bogey.intro.text_4": "Rotational Force can be used to drive Physics Bogies",
	"simurail.ponder.physics_bogey.intro.text_5": "The direction of travel depends on the direction of rotation",
	"simurail.ponder.physics_bogey.intro.text_6": "Provide redstone power to the top to brake",
	"simurail.ponder.physics_bogey.intro.text_7": "Provide redstone power to the sides to turn at track junctions",
	"simurail.ponder.physics_bogey.intro.text_8": "Right click a with an empty hand to configure its physical properties",
	"simurail.ponder.physics_bogey.intro.text_9": "Right click a with an empty hand while sneaking to configure its visual appearance",

	"simurail.ponder.physics_bogey.electric.header": "Driving Physics Bogies with Electricity",
	"simurail.ponder.physics_bogey.electric.text_1": "Catenary Holders mounted on poles carry overhead lines above a Train Track",
	"simurail.ponder.physics_bogey.electric.text_2": "The overhead lines can supply Simulated Contraptions with electricity",
	"simurail.ponder.physics_bogey.electric.text_3": "Connect the overhead lines to the positive terminal of a power source",
	"simurail.ponder.physics_bogey.electric.text_4": "Connect the negative terminal to a Ground Rod",
	"simurail.ponder.physics_bogey.electric.text_5": "2500 V",
	"simurail.ponder.physics_bogey.electric.text_6": "A Simulated Contraption riding on Physics Bogies can collect this electricity",
	"simurail.ponder.physics_bogey.electric.text_7": "A Pantograph collects current as long as it touches the overhead lines",
	"simurail.ponder.physics_bogey.electric.text_8": "Wire the Pantograph to an Electric Motor, whose shaft drives the Physics Bogies",
	"simurail.ponder.physics_bogey.electric.text_9": "Wire the Electric Motor back to a Physics Bogie; Bogies on a Train Track are grounded through the rails, closing the circuit",
	"simurail.ponder.physics_bogey.electric.text_10": "The Electric Motor now provides Rotational Force from electricity alone, without any fuel",
	"simurail.ponder.physics_bogey.electric.text_11": "Physics Bogies with a higher Drive Strength put more stress on the Electric Motor",
	"simurail.ponder.physics_bogey.electric.text_12": "The capacity a Motor provides grows with the square of its voltage, so a stronger train needs a higher line voltage",
	"simurail.ponder.physics_bogey.electric.text_13": "At 2500 V, a single Motor can turn eight Physics Bogies at maximum Drive Strength up to 200 RPM",
	"simurail.ponder.physics_bogey.electric.text_14": "Once the line is live, the Simulated Contraption can travel as far as the catenary reaches",

	"simurail.ponder.physics_bogey.third_rail.header": "Driving Physics Bogies from a Third Rail",
	"simurail.ponder.physics_bogey.third_rail.text_1": "Instead of overhead lines, an electrified third rail can be laid alongside a Train Track using Iron Rail wire",
	"simurail.ponder.physics_bogey.third_rail.text_2": "A Rail Contact Shoe collects current from the third rail",
	"simurail.ponder.physics_bogey.third_rail.text_3": "Wire the Rail Contact Shoe to an Electric Motor, whose shaft drives the Physics Bogies",
	"simurail.ponder.physics_bogey.third_rail.text_4": "Wire the Electric Motor back to a Physics Bogie; Bogies on a Train Track are grounded through the rails, closing the circuit",
	"simurail.ponder.physics_bogey.third_rail.text_5": "The Simulated Contraption keeps collecting current wherever the third rail reaches",

	"simurail.ponder.automatic_coupler.intro.header": "Connecting Structures with Automatic Couplers",
	"simurail.ponder.automatic_coupler.intro.text_1": "Automatic Couplers automatically connect to each other when close together",
	"simurail.ponder.automatic_coupler.intro.text_2": "Provide redstone power to disconnect",
	"simurail.ponder.automatic_coupler.intro.text_3": "Right click with an empty hand to change the length",
	"simurail.ponder.automatic_coupler.intro.text_4": "Right click with a Wrench to change the type",
	"simurail.ponder.automatic_coupler.intro.text_5": "Automatic Couplers of different types cannot connect",

	"simurail.ponder.gangway_frame.intro.header": "Connecting Structures with Gangway Frames",
	"simurail.ponder.gangway_frame.intro.text_1": "Gangway Frames can be used to create walkways",
	"simurail.ponder.gangway_frame.intro.text_2": "Right click a with an empty hand to connect",
	"simurail.ponder.gangway_frame.intro.text_3": "Provide redstone power or right click a with an empty hand to disconnect",
	"simurail.ponder.gangway_frame.intro.text_4": "Connected Gangway Frames extend and retract together",
	"simurail.ponder.gangway_frame.intro.text_5": "Right click with a wrench to change shape and rest length",
	"simurail.ponder.gangway_frame.intro.text_6": "Gangway Frames only connect to matching shapes",

	"simurail.ponder.gangway_frame.coupler.header": "Combining Gangway Frames with Automatic Couplers",
	"simurail.ponder.gangway_frame.coupler.text_1": "Gangway Frames can be combined with Automatic Couplers",
	"simurail.ponder.gangway_frame.coupler.text_2": "Gangway Frames automatically connect and disconnect when Automatic Couplers connect and disconnect",

	"simurail.ponder.connector.intro.header": "Connecting Physics Bogies with the Bogie Connector",
	"simurail.ponder.connector.intro.text_1": "The Bogie Connector is a tool that connects Physics Bogies into a group",
	"simurail.ponder.connector.intro.text_2": "Connected Physics Bogies follow each other at track junctions",
	"simurail.ponder.connector.intro.text_3": "Redstone power can be provided at any connected Physics Bogie to brake or to turn at track junctions",
	"simurail.ponder.connector.intro.text_4": "To disconnect, click the same position twice",

	"simurail.ponder.connector.coupler.header": "Connecting Physics Bogies to Automatic Couplers",
	"simurail.ponder.connector.coupler.text_1": "The Bogie Connector can connect Physics Bogies to Automatic Couplers on the same Simulated Contraption",
	"simurail.ponder.connector.coupler.text_2": "Bogies automatically connects and disconnects when Automatic Couplers connect and disconnect",

	"simurail.ponder.probe_reader.intro.header": "Detecting Track Points using Bogie Probe Readers",
	"simurail.ponder.probe_reader.intro.text_1": "To place a Bogie Probe Reader, select the side of a Physics Bogie to read probe data from, then place it nearby",
	"simurail.ponder.probe_reader.intro.text_2": "The Bogie Probe Reader reads the probe distance of various track points as a redstone signal",
	"simurail.ponder.probe_reader.intro.text_3": "This requires the Probe Distance of the Physics Bogie to be set",
	"simurail.ponder.probe_reader.intro.text_4": "Right click to configure track point mode, name filter, and distance settings",
	"simurail.ponder.probe_reader.intro.text_5": "The Signal modes check for various states of Track Signals",
	"simurail.ponder.probe_reader.intro.text_6": "Signals can be named for the name filter using signs",
	"simurail.ponder.probe_reader.intro.text_7": "The Station modes check for various states of Track Stations",
	"simurail.ponder.probe_reader.intro.text_8": "The Track Discontinuity mode checks for the end of the track",

	"simurail.ponder.remote_controller.intro.header": "Controlling Bogie Behavior using Bogie Remote Controllers",
	"simurail.ponder.remote_controller.intro.text_1": "To place a Bogie Remote Controller, select the a Physics Bogie, then place it nearby",
	"simurail.ponder.remote_controller.intro.text_2": "The Bogie Remote Controller remotely sends redstone signals to a Physics Bogie, controlling and toggling its behavior",
	"simurail.ponder.remote_controller.intro.text_3": "Right click to configure the control mode",
	"simurail.ponder.remote_controller.intro.text_4": "Supply a redstone signal to control the linked Physics Bogie",



	"simurail.ponder.physics_roller.intro.header": "Paving with Physics Rollers",
	"simurail.ponder.physics_roller.intro.text_1": "On simulated contraptions, a Physics Roller can be used to clear and pave the terrain the structure travels over",
	"simurail.ponder.physics_roller.intro.text_2": "Unlike the Mechanical Roller it is a block of its own, mounted anywhere on the structure",
	"simurail.ponder.physics_roller.intro.text_3": "A line of Rollers works for as long as it is given a redstone signal, and can be switched off without disassembling",
	"simurail.ponder.physics_roller.intro.text_4": "It also has to sit roughly level, and only works while the contraption travels along the direction it faces",
	"simurail.ponder.physics_roller.intro.text_5": "Paving material is drawn from a container placed directly above",
	"simurail.ponder.physics_roller.intro.text_6": "Scrolling the mode selector switches between the available roller modes.",
	"simurail.ponder.physics_roller.materials.header": "Managing the Materials of a Roller Line",
	"simurail.ponder.physics_roller.materials.text_1": "The filter slot beside the mode selector picks which of the container's items may be used as pavement",
	"simurail.ponder.physics_roller.materials.text_2": "Either setting applied to one Roller is shared with every other Roller of the same line",
	"simurail.ponder.physics_roller.materials.text_3": "Rollers without a container of their own draw from the closest one along the line that still holds their material",
	"simurail.ponder.physics_roller.materials.text_4": "While a filter is set, blocks broken by the line are collected into the closest container with space",
	"simurail.ponder.physics_roller.materials.text_5": "Storages of your choice will do, a Vault kept stocked and emptied by belts serves a long line just as well",
	"simurail.ponder.mechanical_roller_pave.header": "Clearing and Paving with the Roller",
	"simurail.ponder.mechanical_roller_pave.text_1": "Mechanical rollers help to clean up terrain around tracks or paths",
	"simurail.ponder.mechanical_roller_pave.text_2": "In its default mode, without a material set, it will simply clear blocks like a Drill",
	"simurail.ponder.mechanical_roller_pave.text_3": "While disassembled, a suitable paving material can be specified",
	"simurail.ponder.mechanical_roller_pave.text_4": "Materials can be supplied via chests or barrels attached to the structure",
	"simurail.ponder.mechanical_roller_pave.text_5": "In addition to breaking blocks, it will now replace the layer beneath them",
	"simurail.ponder.mechanical_roller_pave.text_6": "Note that any block destroyed by a roller has a chance not to yield drops",
	"simurail.ponder.mechanical_roller_pave.text_7": "Rollers are especially useful on Trains, but can also be used on most other types of moving contraptions",
	"simurail.ponder.mechanical_roller_fill.header": "Filling terrain with the Roller",
	"simurail.ponder.mechanical_roller_fill.text_1": "While disassembled, rollers can be set to other modes",
	"simurail.ponder.mechanical_roller_fill.text_2": "The 'fill' modes can help to bridge gaps between pavement and terrain",
	"simurail.ponder.mechanical_roller_fill.text_3": "On 'straight fill', they will place simple columns down to the surface",
	"simurail.ponder.mechanical_roller_fill.text_4": "On 'sloped fill', layers placed further down will increase in size",
	"simurail.ponder.mechanical_roller_fill.text_5": "As opposed to 'clear & pave', neither of these modes will cause the rollers to break existing blocks"
}
